      "message": "Rather than 2 ifs, this can better chain into:\n```\n        if let Some(cb) \u003d context_map\n            .get_by_server_id(server_id)\n            .and_then(|server| context_map.get_callback_from_callback_id(server.cbid))\n        {\n            cb.on_service_removed(status, handle);\n        }\n```\nI experimented this locally and it doesn\u0027t currently work.\n\nThe problem is that `get_callback_from_callback_id()` is `\u0026mut self` and returns `Option\u003c\u0026mut\u003e`. Let\u0027s also change this to be `\u0026self` and return `Option\u003c\u0026\u003e`.\n\nBut `Callbacks::get_by_id` is also unnecessarily mut, so let\u0027s also refactor this to provide both `get_by_id` and `get_by_id_mut` so the caller can choose to not use mut when not needed.\n\nMy local experiment shows that the refactor is not that large so let\u0027s do the refactor too (maybe in a separate preceding patch).",
